        body: '**The QRS narrowed. You are not finished.**\n\nSodium bicarbonate does not remove the drug — it competes with it at the channel. As the bolus wears off, or as more drug is absorbed from the gut, the QRS can widen again.\n\n### Continue\n• **Keep the bicarbonate infusion running** (150 mEq/L at 1–3 mL/kg/h). Do not stop it because the QRS looks better.\n• Continuous cardiac monitoring, with a repeat 12-lead ECG at least hourly while the QRS remains abnormal.\n• Blood gas, sodium, potassium, and chloride every 30–60 minutes while on the infusion.\n\n### Admit\n• **Intensive care** for anyone who required bicarbonate for a wide QRS. This is not a telemetry-floor patient.\n• Involve medical toxicology or your poison center for the wean.\n\n### The asymptomatic exposure with a normal ECG\n• Serial tracings are still required. Peak toxicity can lag ingestion by hours, particularly with a sustained-release preparation or with a drug that has anticholinergic properties and slows gut motility.\n• **A single reassuring ECG is not a clearance.**\n\n### Before discharge is ever considered\n• A normal ECG that has stayed normal across serial tracings over an appropriate observation window\n• Off bicarbonate with no rebound widening\n• Psychiatric evaluation if the exposure was intentional\n\n→ [TCA Toxidrome](#/tree/tca-toxidrome)',
